//│ ║  l.315: 	fun rscModOf: rsc module M
//│ ╙──       	                  ^^^^^^^^
//│ ———————————————| Lowered IR |———————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
//│ define rscModOf⁰ as fun rscModOf¹(): ? { return M² }; end


// A written function type's parameter list becomes the definition's own, which has no
// resource-ness to state, so a modifier on that function type is rejected. `kControl` is
// the same shape without one; `kForall` puts a quantifier between the modifier and the
// function type, `kMaybe` uses `rsc?`, and the paramless `declare`d `kDeclared` consumes
// every parameter list its signature has.

:e
fun k: rsc (C) -> C
fun k(x) = x
//│ ╔══[COMPILATION ERROR] Resource modifiers apply to function values, not to a function definition's parameter lists.
